==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|lunching||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|en|lunching}}, of uncertain origin.
Possibly related to {{m|en|lunch}}, q.v. It is unclear which came first. Possibly influenced by {{m|en|nuncheon|t=light snack taken in the afternoon}}. 

The "sausage" sense is probably a shortening of {{m|en|luncheon sausage}} or {{m|en|luncheon meat}}.

